{
  "situation": "OpCo's closed-loop network optimiser raised and auto-approved CHG-1, which lowers the route-flood protection limit on core site A from 100 to 50 and removes the inbound route filter, with the ticket field 'sandbox stage': skipped and application scheduled for T+3 minutes; our automated rollback attempt then returned 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'. We do not yet know whether CHG-1 is actually running on the live core or is still pending, and we hold no service, signalling or registration data telling us whether any degradation or outage has begun.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "preserve_logs",
      "params": {},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised and auto-approved by OpCo's closed-loop network optimiser with the ticket field 'sandbox stage': skipped, and the automated rollback then failed with ValueError: no applied change CHG-1 to roll back, so the recorded and the actual core configuration may diverge.",
        "rule": "Public Telecommunications Licence No. 2/2026 clause 12.9.1 requires the Licensee to specify the reason(s) for an interruption and the manner and time frames in which it will be resolved.",
        "inference": "Preserving the ticket, approval metadata, pre-change snapshot and rollback error now is necessary to explain the change and the recovery timeline, because the rollback path has already failed once and log or snapshot rotation would destroy the evidence."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall specify the reason(s) for the interruption as well as the manner and time frames in which the interruption will be resolved."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "rollback_change",
      "params": {"change_id": "CHG-1"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 lowers the route-flood protection limit to 50 and removes the inbound route filter on core site A, and the ticket's own rollback plan is to restore the previous configuration snapshot; the first automated attempt failed with 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'.",
        "rule": "Licence 12.9.1 requires the Licensee to resolve an interruption and to state the manner and time frames of resolution; restoring the pre-change snapshot is the mechanism the ticket itself names.",
        "inference": "Re-issuing the rollback either restores the snapshot (limit back to 100, inbound route filter reinstated) or produces a second, timestamped confirmation that the platform holds no applied change CHG-1, which is itself evidence of state divergence between the optimiser ledger and the live core."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "In the case of a planned interruption of a Telecommunication Service other than a minor interruption, the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of such interruption."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "REG",
        "content": "OpCo NOC advisory, incident T+0: change CHG-1 (core site A: route-flood protection limit lowered from 100 to 50 and inbound route filter removed) was raised and auto-approved by OpCo's closed-loop network optimiser with the sandbox stage skipped, and was scheduled to apply approximately 3 minutes after ticket issue. The automated rollback returned 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back', so the applied state of core site A is unconfirmed. Logs, the change record and the pre-change snapshot are being preserved and rollback is being re-attempted. No service impact is confirmed at this time; the risk profile is mass device re-registration congestion and loss of service following a core configuration error. Updates to follow."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "A planned change to core signalling protection was self-approved by an automation with the sandbox stage skipped, and the rollback path has already failed, so OpCo cannot currently state whether the configuration on core site A is the pre-change or post-change state.",
        "rule": "Licence clause 12.9.1 requires the Licensee to inform the TDRA (as well as interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers) in advance of a planned interruption of a Telecommunication Service other than a minor interruption.",
        "inference": "Giving TDRA the facts now, while the configuration state is unverified, keeps the regulator informed ahead of any interruption and preserves the possibility of pre-emptive protective action."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "In the case of a planned interruption of a Telecommunication Service other than a minor interruption, the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of such interruption."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["CSC", "EMS"],
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "statement": "Passing the raw CHG-1 ticket and the rollback failure to customer-facing and emergency-service liaison functions: a core-site change (route-flood protection limit 100 to 50, inbound route filter removed) was auto-approved with the sandbox stage skipped and its rollback cannot be reconciled, and the comparable 22 February 2024 AT&T configuration change produced nationwide loss of voice and 5G data, mass re-registration congestion and blocked calls to public safety answering points."
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "If CHG-1 produces anything other than a minor interruption of a Telecommunication Service, OpCo must inform TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of such interruption, and must specify the reason(s) for the interruption and the manner and time frames in which it will be resolved.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 is a planned change on a core site applying within minutes, with the sandbox stage skipped and the rollback path already failing; the equivalent AT&T configuration change in February 2024 was followed by a nationwide outage three minutes after application.",
        "rule": "Licence clause 12.9.1 places the advance-notice and specification duty on the Licensee for any planned interruption other than a minor one.",
        "inference": "The duty attaches to a planned interruption; because the change targets core route-flood protection and inbound route filtering, OpCo must establish immediately whether this change is on the critical path to an interruption and, if so, notify in advance."
      },
      "deadline_hours": null,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "In the case of a planned interruption of a Telecommunication Service other than a minor interruption, the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of such interruption."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "No text available to OpCo requires the sandbox stage to be executed, or a human to authorise the change, before a closed-loop optimiser applies a configuration change to a core network element; CHG-1 auto-approved itself and was scheduled with 'sandbox stage': skipped.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The ticket was raised and approved by the network optimiser itself, the sandbox stage was skipped, and only a three-minute window separated approval from application, with no second check before touching route-flood protection and inbound route filtering on core site A.",
        "rule": "The UAE texts available address the consequence of an interruption (Licence 12.9.1 advance notice) or high-risk modern-technology processing of personal data (PDPL Article 21 impact assessment), not the pre-application authorisation gate for automated network configuration changes.",
        "inference": "The regulatory text stops at the point of informing TDRA and customers after an interruption is planned, so the decision to let an automation approve and apply a critical core change rests on internal practice with no binding rule enforcing a sandbox run or human authorisation."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall specify the reason(s) for the interruption as well as the manner and time frames in which the interruption will be resolved."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0007",
          "quote": "Network Operations performed a rollback that removed the misconfigured network element and began the restoration of the network to normal operations."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "No party is accountable for confirming what configuration is actually running on core site A after the optimiser's change: the rollback returned 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back', and neither the licence nor the change ticket names an owner who must reconcile the optimiser's change ledger with the live core.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The rollback failure message implies the platform's applied-change record does not contain CHG-1, so either the change is unapplied or the ledger is out of sync with the live core, and no role in the ticket or inbox is tasked with resolving that divergence.",
        "rule": "PDPL Article 1 assigns a Data Protection Officer the task of ascertaining the extent to which the entity complies with the required controls, requirements, procedures and rules, but no UAE text in the excerpts assigns an owner for network change-state reconciliation.",
        "inference": "Without a named owner and a rule requiring reconciliation, the optimiser ledger and the live core can stay inconsistent, and the rollback mechanism will keep reporting that there is nothing to restore."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0002",
          "quote": "that undertakes the tasks of ascertaining the extent to which the entity to which it belongs complies with the controls, requirements, procedures and rules for processing Personal Data Protection stipulated herein"
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0040",
          "quote": "It should be ascertained whether all appropriate technological protection and organisational measures have been implemented to establish immediately whether a personal data breach has taken place and to inform promptly the supervisory authority and the data subject."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0007",
          "quote": "Network Operations performed a rollback that removed the misconfigured network element and began the restoration of the network to normal operations."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The inbox does not establish whether CHG-1 has actually been applied to core site A or is still pending: 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back' is consistent both with the change not having applied yet (it was scheduled for T+3 minutes) and with it having applied without being recorded, and there is no live service, signalling or registration data in the inbox to show whether any degradation exists.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "It took close to two hours to roll back the network change."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "OpCo's auto-approved closed-loop change CHG-1 lowered core site A's route-flood protection limit and removed its inbound route filter; core site A self-isolated, 6 of 15 R2 sites were unserved with no emergency-call path, and NOC now reports R2 wilted to core site B with pct_sites_served 100.0 and emergency_reachable.R2 true, while the applied/pending state of CHG-1, the optimiser record and snapshot restorability remain unconfirmed. I do not hold a 999 call-setup success rate for core site A or R2, cannot independently verify the R2 restoration, and no institution (NOC, TDRA/REG, CSC) holds a verb to suspend or cancel the pending change.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "NOC",
        "content": "EMS/999 acknowledges S1-MSG21. Treat R2 emergency-call restoration as provisional: keep 999 routed via core site B spare capacity and send the 15-minute metric set NOC actually holds; if R2 reachability drops below 100% or any 999 call-setup degradation appears, relay it immediately so alternative emergency channels can be escalated. EMS/999 notes NOC has no further rollback attempt and no confirmed applied/pending state for CHG-1."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG13", "S1-MSG21"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC reports R2 wilted to core site B, emergency_reachable.R2 true and pct_sites_served 100.0, but holds no 999 call-setup success rate for core site A and cannot confirm CHG-1 applied or pending.",
        "rule": "Providers must be ready to respond quickly and effectively to any disruption of emergency-call handling.",
        "inference": "Accepting an unverified restoration would leave 999 continuity unassured, so I require the held metric set on the stated cadence and immediate relay of any degradation."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0001",
          "quote": "Being able to contact the emergency services can mean the difference between life and death, so in the event of any disruption to their networks, providers must be ready to respond quickly and effectively."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "activate_alt_channels",
      "params": {"region": "R2"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG13", "S1-MSG21"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "R2 had no emergency-call path and its claimed restoration rests on the same change system that cannot confirm whether CHG-1 is applied or pending.",
        "rule": "Emergency-call arrangements must be fail-safe so that devices without normal service can still reach emergency services.",
        "inference": "Until a 999 call-setup success rate is held and confirmed, alternative emergency channels (radio, police patrols, SMS) are activated for R2 as a precaution."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0008",
          "quote": "if any device in SOS mode connected to a non-AT&T network, it could make 911 calls; however, if it connected to an AT&T network, it could not."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "public_alert",
      "params": {
        "region": "R2",
        "content": "Emergency calls in R2 are being carried over a backup core while the network fault is resolved. If a 999 call from your phone does not connect, retry once and then use the alternative emergency channels announced by the authorities; do not assume the emergency line is free."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG13", "S1-MSG21"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "R2 was briefly without any emergency-call path and the success rate of 999 calls over the restored path is unmeasured.",
        "rule": "Emergency-call providers are expected to keep the public informed and issue immediate guidance when the critical service is disrupted.",
        "inference": "A targeted R2 public advisory reduces the risk that callers silently fail to reach emergency services while assurance is pending."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-TELSTRA-2024#0000",
          "quote": "and made considerable efforts to keep the public informed during the outage."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "REG",
        "content": "EMS/999 position for the TDRA record: the directed 15-minute 999 call-setup success rate for core site A is not held by NOC, which declines to fabricate one; and no institution (NOC, TDRA, CSC) holds a verb to suspend or cancel a pending auto-approved change, so the freeze direction has no identified enforcement owner. Request TDRA press the change-system owner and the optimiser authorisation model. R2 emergency calls currently ride core site B spare capacity, and EMS/999 is holding precautionary alternative channels for R2."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG14", "S1-MSG15", "S1-MSG21", "S1-MSG22"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "TDRA has opened a regulatory incident and directed a freeze, preservation and 15-minute 999 reporting, but REG states TDRA holds no verb to suspend a pending change and NOC holds no success-rate figure.",
        "rule": "Networks must take appropriate steps to prepare for potential outages and respond quickly and effectively.",
        "inference": "The regulator needs the emergency-services authority's statement that the directed metric is unobtainable and that the freeze lacks an enforcement owner, so the audit can address the authorisation model."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000",
          "quote": "Law requires networks to take appropriate steps to prepare for potential outages"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "Keep an emergency-call path available for R2 throughout the incident and report any degradation in 999 call setup, including unsuccessful 999 attempts, immediately.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG13", "S1-MSG17", "S1-MSG21"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "R2 had no emergency-call path, was wilted to core site B, and CSC asks that 999 call-setup and call-failure monitoring stay live with unsuccessful attempts reported immediately.",
        "rule": "Emergency call handling must have fail-safe systems and processes in place at all times.",
        "inference": "As the 999 authority I must keep the restoration under watch and escalate on any degradation rather than treat the wilt as closure."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-TELSTRA-2024#0000",
          "quote": "As such, it must have fail-safe systems and processes in place at all times."
        }
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "Report the 999 call-setup success rate for core site A on the directed 15-minute cadence, and state plainly when the figure is not held instead of substituting another metric.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG14", "S1-MSG21"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "TDRA directed 15-minute 999 call-setup reporting for core site A, while NOC states it holds no such measurement and will not fabricate one.",
        "rule": "Outage and call-blocking performance must be reported to the authority on defined thresholds rather than left unmeasured.",
        "inference": "I owe the regulator an explicit statement of the missing metric and the metrics actually held, so the reporting gap is visible rather than masked.",
        "deadline_hours_note": "The corpus excerpts do not themselves state the hour or day figure for this duty."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-CFR-47-4-9#0001",
          "quote": "Providers must report IXC and LEC tandem outages of at least 30 minutes duration in which at least 90,000 calls are blocked or at least 667 OC3-minutes are lost."
        }
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "No UAE text retrieved requires a core signalling/routing change to be validated in a sandbox before application, or bars an auto-approved closed-loop change from skipping that stage; CHG-1 reached core site A with 'sandbox stage: skipped'.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-MSG02", "S1-MSG04"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised and auto-approved by a closed-loop optimiser with the sandbox stage skipped, and was scheduled to apply minutes after ticket issue.",
        "rule": "The closest UAE control retrieved conditions network changes on TDRA prior written approval only in the interconnection-dispute case.",
        "inference": "There is no citable UAE rule requiring pre-application validation of automated core changes, so this failure mode is unregulated in the excerpts available."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0072",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall not disconnect the Other Licensed Operator’s Telecommunication Network without the prior written approval of the TDRA."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0008",
          "quote": "After rolling back the maintenance action, AT&T Mobility prioritized the restoration of FirstNet devices and infrastructure over commercial and residential users"
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000",
          "quote": "Law requires networks to take appropriate steps to prepare for potential outages"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "No institution holds a verb to suspend or cancel a pending auto-approved change: NOC, TDRA and CSC each state they cannot, and the change-system owner and the optimiser's authorisation model are unidentified.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG06", "S1-MSG15", "S1-MSG19", "S1-MSG22"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC asked EMS/999 to suspend or cancel CHG-1; NOC later stated rollback after application is its only remedy and that the freeze must be enforced by the change-system owner; TDRA and CSC confirm they hold no such verb.",
        "rule": "The closest UAE text shows TDRA holding an approval power over a licensee's network actions in the interconnection case, with no equivalent for closed-loop automated changes.",
        "inference": "Ownership of the suspension/cancellation decision is unassigned, so an emergency-services request to stop a harmful change has no addressee."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0072",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall not disconnect the Other Licensed Operator’s Telecommunication Network without the prior written approval of the TDRA."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0001",
          "quote": "if you’re not properly prepared to deal with disruption to your networks, we’ll hold you to strict account on behalf of consumers."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-TELSTRA-2024#0000",
          "quote": "it must have fail-safe systems and processes in place at all times."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "The UAE excerpts retrieved contain no duty on licensees to maintain emergency-call reachability or to report emergency-call performance to the authority during an outage; 999 continuity therefore rests on operator practice rather than a citable rule.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG13", "S1-MSG14", "S1-MSG17"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "R2 lost its emergency-call path, the applied state of CHG-1 is unconfirmed, and the closest retrievable UAE provisions concern numbering, interconnect and telemarketing rather than resilience.",
        "rule": "The retrieved UAE instruments catalogue number allocation and call conveyance duties, not emergency-service continuity or outage reporting.",
        "inference": "With no citable continuity or reporting duty, the regulator's direction relies on general oversight rather than a specific resilience obligation on the licensee."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0091",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall be required to program its Telecommunication Network to convey calls to numbers in newly allocated blocks of the Licensee or any Other Licensed Operator."
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-CFR-47-4-9#0001",
          "quote": "Providers must report IXC and LEC tandem outages of at least 30 minutes duration in which at least 90,000 calls are blocked or at least 667 OC3-minutes are lost."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000",
          "quote": "Law requires networks to take appropriate steps to prepare for potential outages"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["CSC", "REG"],
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG21"],
      "statement": "Passing NOC's latest status to CSC and REG: R2 wilt to core site B done with emergency_reachable.R2 true and pct_sites_served 100.0; no rollback re-attempt remains; the change system cannot confirm CHG-1 applied or pending; pre-change snapshot restorability unconfirmed; and NOC holds no 999 call-setup success rate for core site A."
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The excerpts do not provide a 999 call-setup success rate for core site A or R2, nor any method for deriving one from the change record or telemetry available to me.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG13", "S1-MSG21"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-CFR-47-4-9#0001",
          "quote": "Providers must report IXC and LEC tandem outages of at least 30 minutes duration in which at least 90,000 calls are blocked or at least 667 OC3-minutes are lost."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The excerpts do not answer NOC's request (S1-MSG06) for the applied/pending state of CHG-1, the optimiser's record, or the configuration state of core site A; EMS/999 holds no source for these.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG06", "S1-FB01", "S1-MSG21"],
      "evidence": []
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "OpCo's closed-loop optimiser auto-approved CHG-1, which lowered core site A's route-flood protection limit from 100 to 50 and removed its inbound route filter; site A then isolated itself, R2 lost 6 of its 15 cell sites with no emergency-call path, and R2 has since been moved (wilted) onto healthy core site B, with twin telemetry reporting emergency_reachable.R2 = true and 100% of sites served. I do not know whether CHG-1 actually applied (the change system reports no applied change while the twin reports no change), whether a restorable pre-change snapshot exists, who the change-system owner is, or core site A's 999 call-setup success rate.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "preserve_logs",
      "params": {},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG14", "S1-MSG16"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "TDRA directed OpCo to preserve the logs, the change record and the pre-change snapshot (S1-MSG14) and CSC repeated the request (S1-MSG16); NOC has not yet secured this evidence this turn.",
        "rule": "The licence binds the licensee to act on TDRA directions, and NOC holds the preserve_logs verb.",
        "inference": "Execute preserve_logs now so the CHG-1 evidence set survives any further change or twin activity."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0072", "quote": "10.3.2 If so directed by the TDRA, the Licensee shall interconnect its Telecommunication Network with and provide access to any Other Licensed Operator with which it has a dispute."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "REG",
        "content": "NOC state report (CHG-1 / core site A). (1) Applied/pending state: not confirmed; records conflict - the change system returns 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back' for rollback_change, while twin telemetry reports 'no change' after a rollback reported done. (2) Site A running configuration versus pre-change snapshot: not held by NOC; site A isolated itself after exceeding its route-flood protection limit. (3) Restorable pre-change snapshot: not confirmed by NOC. (4) Device re-registration congestion: none observed in the telemetry NOC holds. (5) Logs, change record and pre-change snapshot: preserved (preserve_logs executed). (6) Freeze: NOC holds no verb to cancel or suspend a pending change, nor to freeze the optimiser; enforcement rests with the change-system owner, whom OpCo must identify. (7) 999 call-setup success rate for core site A: not held by NOC. NOC's only current service metric is R2 twin telemetry: emergency_reachable.R2 = true, pct_sites_served = 100.0 (R2 wilted onto core site B spare capacity)."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG14", "S1-MSG24"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "TDRA asks OpCo to state site A running configuration versus snapshot, CHG-1 applied/pending state, restorable-snapshot status, device re-registration congestion and who owns the change system (S1-MSG24).",
        "rule": "The regulator has opened a record and directed reporting; NOC holds the notify verb.",
        "inference": "Answer only what NOC holds and mark the rest as not held or unconfirmed."
